WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.079 --> 00:00:00.912
- Boozy cereal?

00:00:00.912 --> 00:00:01.745
- Bring that to Brooklyn,

00:00:01.745 --> 00:00:03.074
white people from all over will be like--

00:00:03.074 --> 00:00:04.119
- Oh my gosh!

00:00:04.119 --> 00:00:05.048
- Oh my god.

00:00:05.048 --> 00:00:08.631
- You better leave this
out the video, man.

00:00:10.876 --> 00:00:12.095
- Hey guys, my name is Delisa,

00:00:12.095 --> 00:00:13.674
I'm from Texas, and where I come from,

00:00:13.674 --> 00:00:15.346
we like to enjoy some boozy cereal.

00:00:15.346 --> 00:00:17.633
So I asked around the office
if anybody has tried it,

00:00:17.633 --> 00:00:19.549
and no one seems to know
what I'm talking about.

00:00:19.549 --> 00:00:21.894
So I'm gonna let them know
how we do it in the South.

00:00:21.894 --> 00:00:24.175
The only thing is, they
don't know what's coming.

00:00:24.175 --> 00:00:25.008
(record scratch)

00:00:25.008 --> 00:00:26.808
- Spiked milk, like, are we getting drunk?

00:00:26.808 --> 00:00:27.643
- What?

00:00:27.643 --> 00:00:29.312
- It's not even 11 o'clock.

00:00:29.312 --> 00:00:30.895
Yo, I've got a job.

00:00:34.397 --> 00:00:36.022
- [Interviewer] Bon appetit.

00:00:36.022 --> 00:00:37.450
- I don't know, it tastes kind of like

00:00:37.450 --> 00:00:39.865
regular milk to me,
which is gonna be weird

00:00:39.865 --> 00:00:41.328
if it's spiked with a lot of alcohol.

00:00:41.328 --> 00:00:43.290
- There's a faint sock taste.

00:00:43.290 --> 00:00:45.078
- Fruity, fruity, fruity
loop, fruity loop...

00:00:45.078 --> 00:00:46.495
- Now I taste it.

00:00:46.495 --> 00:00:48.039
- It tastes like Froot Loops.

00:00:48.039 --> 00:00:49.165
But then the back of my mouth is like,

00:00:49.165 --> 00:00:51.082
that tastes like vodka.

00:00:53.252 --> 00:00:55.968
- Like, there's a slight
aftertaste of alcohol,

00:00:55.968 --> 00:00:57.721
but it's not upsetting me.

00:00:57.721 --> 00:00:59.800
Like, it's not gonna stop me from going

00:00:59.800 --> 00:01:01.216
through this whole bowl right now.

00:01:01.216 --> 00:01:03.515
- This is the classiest one,
I'd say, of all of them.

00:01:03.515 --> 00:01:05.558
- You can find me on
Twitter, @IAmDisgusted

00:01:05.558 --> 00:01:07.474
because I am disgusted.

00:01:07.474 --> 00:01:09.146
- I feel like this is
great for spring break

00:01:09.146 --> 00:01:11.688
with your friends, like
we're gonna be day drinkin'

00:01:11.688 --> 00:01:15.021
so let's turn up with some drunk cereal.

00:01:17.366 --> 00:01:18.616
- This is milk?

00:01:20.361 --> 00:01:22.660
- I'm really bad at tasting booze in milk.

00:01:22.660 --> 00:01:24.204
Like, I think this is why White Russians

00:01:24.204 --> 00:01:26.746
became a thing, is because it's hidden.

00:01:26.746 --> 00:01:28.116
- This tastes like dinner.

00:01:28.116 --> 00:01:30.996
Like roasted chicken and, like,

00:01:30.996 --> 00:01:33.968
rice and peas and string beans.

00:01:33.968 --> 00:01:35.001
- Are you sure?

00:01:35.001 --> 00:01:36.127
- Yeah.

00:01:36.127 --> 00:01:38.716
- I usually think alcohol ruins things,

00:01:38.716 --> 00:01:40.423
so I'm so surprised.

00:01:40.423 --> 00:01:42.722
Maybe it's just like you
put the right amount in.

00:01:42.722 --> 00:01:43.848
- Now it tastes like ham.

00:01:43.848 --> 00:01:46.181
And collard greens.

00:01:46.181 --> 00:01:49.811
- This is really good,
this is like #adulting.

00:01:49.811 --> 00:01:51.476
- I don't know if it's
because I'm excited,

00:01:51.476 --> 00:01:53.391
but I kind of feel drunk already.

00:01:53.391 --> 00:01:55.400
- At night, as soon as five o'clock hits,

00:01:55.400 --> 00:01:56.480
I might like this.

00:01:56.480 --> 00:01:58.813
But right now I can't do it.

00:02:00.613 --> 00:02:02.157
- I can't taste anything besides

00:02:02.157 --> 00:02:04.119
Cinnamon Toast Crunch right now.

00:02:04.119 --> 00:02:05.152
- That's a good thing, though.

00:02:05.152 --> 00:02:07.254
- Honey Jack and French toast?

00:02:07.254 --> 00:02:09.158
That's like a match made in heaven, yo.

00:02:09.158 --> 00:02:11.584
- Wheaties are no longer
the breakfast of champions.

00:02:11.584 --> 00:02:13.291
Drunk Cinnamon Toast Crunch.

00:02:13.291 --> 00:02:15.462
- I would eat this on the beach.

00:02:15.462 --> 00:02:19.129
In my finery, just,
like, this and a Speedo.

00:02:21.720 --> 00:02:24.727
- See, I really wanna throw
a breakfast party now,

00:02:24.727 --> 00:02:26.433
where I invite my friends over,

00:02:26.433 --> 00:02:29.347
we watch crappy cartoons,
and get drunk off cereal

00:02:29.347 --> 00:02:30.683
and just have fun.

00:02:30.683 --> 00:02:32.227
These cereals, they're great.

00:02:32.227 --> 00:02:33.736
- I love breakfast, I love booze.

00:02:33.736 --> 00:02:36.104
Breakfast, booze, cereal, milk, love it!

00:02:36.104 --> 00:02:37.370
Alcohol, awesome!

00:02:37.370 --> 00:02:39.153
- I do feel it

00:02:39.153 --> 00:02:40.603
in here,

00:02:40.603 --> 00:02:41.619
right now.

00:02:41.619 --> 00:02:44.405
- Next time I go to the club,
this is what I'm gonna bring.

00:02:44.405 --> 00:02:46.367
You just need to put
your milk in the flask,

00:02:46.367 --> 00:02:48.700
